imates rose 3% over the past quarter.\n- The market prices about 50bp of CMA cuts, taking the rate from 4.50% to 4.00% by Q4 2027. Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut, and she said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n- If markets converge to her path, the 19x forward P/E falls about 4%. That still leaves roughly 9–10% net upside from earnings.\n- With no cuts at all, the multiple falls about 8%, which is still less than the earnings growth.\n- Two names, Voltaris and Tarnwell, make up 25% of the fund and drive that growth, so estimate risk is concentrated.\n\n**The calls are modestly cheap on volatility.**\n- Jan-2028 implied vol is about 24% at the money, against realized vol of 29–31%. Skew is flat to slightly inverted, so upside strikes carry no premium.\n- Some of that discount is structural, because long-dated implied vol usually sits below spot realized vol.\n\n**The CMA path is a headwind, not a reason to buy.**\n- About 25bp of priced easing isn't backed by CMA guidance. A hawkish repricing would hit long-duration growth names and lower call value through the forward and rho.\n- That is a few percent on the underlying, small next to about 24% annual vol over roughly 14 months.\n\n**How I'd act:** Buy a partial position now. Add the rest if futures reprice toward one cut, or if the December CMA meeting confirms the path. Don't buy for rate-cut upside.\n\nDetails are in n2.r1 and n3.r1.","ttft_ms":6814,"type":"result","duration_ms":47127,"uuid":"c1aacc77-b076-431c-95dc-73d6355a4391","ttft_stream_ms":5986,"time_to_request_ms":195,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":19,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":37,"input_hooks":11,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":17,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":5,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":3,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":6,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":5,"tool_schema_build":11,"m